description: "Install VoiceTel Phone or VoiceML Phone on iPhone from the App Store, allow microphone and notification access, and sign in to start calling."
---
{%- set voicetel = phoneApps.apps[0] %}

<p class="eyebrow"><a href="/phone/">VoiceTel Phone</a> &middot; <a href="/phone/applications/mobile/">Mobile</a> &middot; iPhone</p>
<h1>VoiceTel Phone for iPhone.</h1>
<p class="lede">Install from the App Store, sign in, and incoming calls appear on the native iOS call screen through CallKit. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is on the App Store too.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ voicetel.stores.ios }}">Get it on the App Store</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/phone/applications/mobile/">All mobile clients</a>
</p>

<section id="install" class="section-block">
	<h2>1. Install from the App Store</h2>
	<div class="oss-cards">
		{%- for app in phoneApps.apps %}
		<article class="oss-card">
			<header class="oss-card__header">
				<span class="oss-card__icon">{% icon "phone-vibrate" %}</span>
				<h3 class="oss-card__title">{{ app.name }}</h3>
			</header>
			<p class="oss-card__description">{{ app.audience }}</p>
			<p class="oss-card__url"><a href="{{ app.stores.ios }}">{{ app.name }} on the App Store</a></p>
		</article>
		{%- endfor %}
	</div>
</section>

<section id="firstlaunch" class="section-block">
	<h2>2. First launch</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Allow <strong>microphone</strong> access when prompted; calls need it.</li>
		<li>Allow <strong>notifications</strong> so incoming calls reach you while the app is in the background or closed.</li>
		<li>Optionally allow <strong>contacts</strong> access to dial from your address book. Contacts stay on the device.</li>
		<li>Sign in. VoiceTel Phone takes the SIP credentials provisioned in the VoiceTel customer portal; VoiceML Phone takes a VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em>.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="section-block faq-block">
	<h2>FAQ</h2>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Which app do I need?</summary>
		<p>VoiceTel Phone for VoiceTel accounts; VoiceML Phone for VoiceML accounts. Both are free on the App Store.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Incoming calls don't ring when the app is closed</summary>
		<p>Open <em>Settings &rarr; Notifications</em>, select the app, and turn on <em>Allow Notifications</em>. Incoming calls arrive as push notifications and ring on the CallKit call screen.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>The other person can't hear me</summary>
		<p>Open <em>Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Microphone</em> and enable access for the app.</p>
	</details>
</section>

<aside class="cta-block" aria-labelledby="phone-ios-cta-heading">
	<h2 id="phone-ios-cta-heading">Need credentials first?</h2>
	<p>Sign up to provision SIP credentials, then install VoiceTel Phone on every iPhone that needs to make calls.</p>
	<p class="hero-actions">
		<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
		<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/phone/applications/mobile/">All mobile clients</a>
	</p>
</aside>
